# End-user Changelog

`RelicTracker/RelicTracker.json` → `Changelog` is shown to players in Dalamud. Always write it for them.

## Do

- Short bullets: what changed for the player, in plain language
- Prefer outcomes over implementation ("smoother in Eureka", "Craft with Artisan works again")
- Keep prior player-facing bullets when bumping; lead with the newest release notes
- Match tone of existing good bullets (progress, inventory, right-click, Cosmic tools)

## Don't

- Developer jargon: IPC, ordinals, dedupe, merge, refactor, shared loading, resolver, partials
- Internal names unless players see them (Allagan Tools / Artisan / FFXIV Collect are OK)
- Commit-style or PR-style summaries

## Examples

```text
❌ Cleanup: shared data loading, merged job resolver, deduped quest-reward UI
✅ Under-the-hood tidy; same features, nothing you need to reconfigure

❌ Artisan craft button uses step IDs (needs Artisan with GetRelicToolListId(int, int))
✅ Craft with Artisan works with the latest Artisan relic craft lists

❌ Inventory spam no longer rebuilds all relic ownership every tick
✅ Less stuttering in busy zones like Eureka Hydatos when loot is flying
```
